<title>SOUTH KOREA: Bank of Korea buys dlrs in 1-year forward-dealers.</title>
<headline>Bank of Korea buys dlrs in 1-year forward-dealers.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The central Bank of Korea intervened in one-year forward trading in Wednesday afternoon trade, buying about $20 million at 905 won, dealers said.</p>
<p>The central bank has never confirmed its intervention.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the won fell to 888.60 at 0456 GMT after opening the afternoon session at 888.20.</p>
<p>They said the central bank intervenened to halt a rise in the local currency against the dollar.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
